{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres","id":557698,"title":"Second Edition Ogres","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-16T18:47:53-07:00","id":557698,"title":"Second Edition Ogres","content":"Here's room for chatter on Ogres.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-ogres/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-th...edition-ogres/</a>You can find the draft here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 06-16-2015, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T19:38:49-07:00","id":557743,"title":"","content":"Well, this is one hell of a hard to take Seeming. In the emotional way.<br /> <br /> Then again they all are, but Ogres just seem to have a lot of weight in how violence is escape from both Arcadia and the pain you cause yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T19:40:37-07:00","id":557746,"title":"","content":"I suppose you might say Ogres dwell in the Hurt Locker ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T19:44:26-07:00","id":557750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=557743#post557743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is one hell of a hard to take Seeming. In the emotional way.<br /> <br /> Then again they all are, but Ogres just seem to have a lot of weight in how violence is escape from both Arcadia and the pain you cause yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. This is one of those places where I really wanted to bring some of the metaphors to light in a new way. It's going to be a gut-wrencher for some. But, then again, Changeling's a sensitive game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T19:51:16-07:00","id":557752,"title":"","content":"I've spent a lot of years trying to move away from this sort of thing as a person. It's rewarding to see it captured just right, and in a way 1E couldn't quite capture either.*<br /> <br /> *Though, to be fair, I am wiser and more self-aware now than I was in 2007.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T20:11:59-07:00","id":557763,"title":"","content":"In the Hurt Locker? Ogres are the Hurt locker. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T20:38:17-07:00","id":557782,"title":"","content":"They're like a Viva Puff. Hard chocolate outside, but marshmallow in the middle, but they refuse to believe they have any fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T20:39:55-07:00","id":557784,"title":"","content":"I was not expecting &quot;I'm A Survivor&quot; to start playing in my head after reading the first paragraph.<br /> <br /> Also, what AA said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T20:41:08-07:00","id":557787,"title":"","content":"*One, two, three, four...*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mZ2ZWLXvZ3Y\" data-code=\"mZ2ZWLXvZ3Y\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/mZ2ZWLXvZ3Y/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T20:41:17-07:00","id":557788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=557784#post557784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was not expecting &quot;I'm A Survivor&quot; to start playing in my head after reading the first paragraph.<br /> <br /> Also, what AA said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyonce is always the answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T21:41:32-07:00","id":557861,"title":"","content":"I love this Seeming concept. The bit about replacing their hearts especially.<br /> <br /> My only quibble would be that the mention of Ogres using &quot;brutal social rhetoric&quot; seems contradicted by &quot;Ogres aren't especially good at communicating with words.&quot; It seems to me like they could be good with words, but would be inclined to use those words to hurt (like an insult comic or a dirt-slinging politician).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T21:55:07-07:00","id":557866,"title":"","content":"Maybe the line &quot;Suffice to say, Ogres aren't especially good at communicating with words,&quot; could be replaced with something like &quot;Even when she's trying to be civil, the temptation to resort to violence to get her point across is always there.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T22:13:09-07:00","id":557906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=557866#post557866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the line &quot;Suffice to say, Ogres aren't especially good at communicating with words,&quot; could be replaced with something like &quot;Even when she's trying to be civil, the temptation to resort to violence to get her point across is always there.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure sure. I get that read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T22:53:21-07:00","id":557918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=557752#post557752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've spent a lot of years trying to move away from this sort of thing as a person. It's rewarding to see it captured just right, and in a way 1E couldn't quite capture either.*<br /> <br /> *Though, to be fair, I am wiser and more self-aware now than I was in 2007.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly this. As person that were bullied all his life - even if I look as typical Ogre myself - and having some slightly violent tendencies, I can totally agree with this Seeming, in darker parts of mine soul. It's hard lessons, not pleasant ones - but very true to our day to day lives.<br /> <br /> As general, beside being great Seeming, <b>I'm very found of new format - three shorter character concepts get a lot better view how Ogres can be diverse and different!</b> I only wish other Seemings will be re-written in this manner in 2nd Draft. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T23:07:33-07:00","id":557922,"title":"","content":"...The other three had three example characters too. ._.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T23:10:32-07:00","id":557925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=557918#post557918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As general, beside being great Seeming, <b>I'm very found of new format - three shorter character concepts get a lot better view how Ogres can be diverse and different!</b> I only wish other Seemings will be re-written in this manner in 2nd Draft. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand. These are significantly longer than the concepts featured in Beasts. Slightly longer than Darklings. Right about the exact same size as Fairest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T23:30:15-07:00","id":557932,"title":"","content":"There is a need to clear something up, I think, about the Curse, since how efficaciously that pain is communicated is a touch unspecified and it could ostensibly apply to the very violence that applies to the Seeming Blessing.<br /> <br /> If an Ogre breaks a man's hand to get him to turn over his wallet, and the man gives an ear-splitting shriek of pain, then whimpers in tears, curling up holding their hand, the Ogre could gain and lose Clarity in the same breath for the same act. Indeed, it would seem harder to find examples where this couldn't happen than where it could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T23:32:27-07:00","id":557933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=557925#post557925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I understand. These are significantly longer than the concepts featured in Beasts. Slightly longer than Darklings. Right about the exact same size as Fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the number of concepts as opposed to the length is the thing - I remember Darklings especially being criticised because the one character example was taken as the sole representative of the Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T23:35:13-07:00","id":557934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=557932#post557932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a need to clear something up, I think, about the Curse, since how efficaciously that pain is communicated is a touch unspecified and it could ostensibly apply to the very violence that applies to the Seeming Blessing.<br /> <br /> If an Ogre breaks a man's hand to get him to turn over his wallet, and the man gives an ear-splitting shriek of pain, then whimpers in tears, curling up holding their hand, the Ogre could gain and lose Clarity in the same breath for the same act. Indeed, it would seem harder to find examples where this couldn't happen than where it could.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're confused (or I am):<br /> <br /> The Blessing kicks in when <b>you </b>threaten or use violence on <b>someone else</b>.<br /> <br /> The Curse kicks in when <b>someone else</b> points out <b>you</b> have been hurt.<br /> <br /> So unless the screams literally shatter your ear drum and then someone points that out to you via sign-language you are good to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T23:36:39-07:00","id":557935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=557933#post557933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the number of concepts as opposed to the length is the thing - I remember Darklings especially being criticised because the one character example was taken as the sole representative of the Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there are three in each and every one I've posted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T00:32:50-07:00","id":557984,"title":"","content":"Hm, I went back and checked and you're right.<br /> <br /> I literally don't know how I got that impression, but I remember it being quite distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T00:46:05-07:00","id":558011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=557935#post557935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there are three in each and every one I've posted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given my posting history on the subject perhaps I'm in a good position to explain. The &quot;one example charachter&quot; people are remembering is actually the Background and the Escape section of the Darkling write up.<br /> <br /> In the Darkling write up it really felt like Background and Escape were describing one specific person. The Ogre write up's background section describes the <i>situation</i> Ogres were in (bully victim) rather than their charachter traits (The Darkling backgrounds talks about them as loyal people). As a result it doesn't feel so much like a single charachter.<br /> <br /> That's why you have Xenesis and WyrdHampster praising the new format. It's not a new format, but it still feels like it.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <br /> Now onto my thoughts about the Seming.<br /> <br /> Firstly, I love the core concept that an Ogre escapes by tearing out their heart, and with it their compassion.<br /> <br /> As I said above. I feel my complaint about the background section still holds, if to a lesser extent. Bullying victims are a natural fit for Ogres, but I still very much prefer the idea that you could go through the entire charachter arc of: bullied -&gt; grow armour -&gt; remove own heart; entirely in Arcadia. A guy who was never bullied in his life but had an emotionally abusive lover for a Keeper is more likely to end up an Ogre than a long time bullying victim who ended up a slave in the mines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T00:52:53-07:00","id":558015,"title":"","content":"Hey MachineIV,<br /> <br /> Thinking about our brief conversation in the Court Creation thread. Do you think our differing opinions here are also stemming from a myself looking at things from an in charachter literal perspective while you &amp; the Seeming writer are looking at things more metaphorically.<br /> <br /> I.E. You're giving Ogres a background as bullying victims because they're a metaphor for the bullying victims that grow up to become bullies themselves.<br /> <br /> I'm saying that from a literal in charachter perspective anybody could develop into an Ogre if their Durance pushed them in that direction; and so the background incorect - you don't need to have been bullied before Arcadia; emotional bullying inside Arcadia is sufficient.<br /> <br /> Does that sound plausible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T01:16:02-07:00","id":558018,"title":"","content":"Still, I find the Blessing far easier to trigger and with less consequences than the previous ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T01:18:20-07:00","id":558019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558015#post558015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey MachineIV,<br /> <br /> Thinking about our brief conversation in the Court Creation thread. Do you think our differing opinions here are also stemming from a myself looking at things from an in charachter literal perspective while you &amp; the Seeming writer are looking at things more metaphorically.<br /> <br /> I.E. You're giving Ogres a background as bullying victims because they're a metaphor for the bullying victims that grow up to become bullies themselves.<br /> <br /> I'm saying that from a literal in charachter perspective anybody could develop into an Ogre if their Durance pushed them in that direction; and so the background incorect - you don't need to have been bullied before Arcadia; emotional bullying inside Arcadia is sufficient.<br /> <br /> Does that sound plausible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure. I think in these cases, she's flavourfully presenting a &quot;core example&quot; of a character that fits the mold pretty strongly. IE: This is showing you what a character is like, if that character is defined by her Seeming. Not every character is. In these examples, it's a facet of the character that's permeated every bit of her concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T01:29:57-07:00","id":558021,"title":"","content":"Ogres don't need to have been bullied. They can just feel like they were. There are a growing number of people that seek out the role of victim. They <i>want</i> to be a victim so badly they will create delusions of abuse. Joke is on them once they find themselves in Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T06:09:22-07:00","id":558148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558018#post558018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I find the Blessing far easier to trigger and with less consequences than the previous ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because punching people in the face all the time has absolutely no effect on how people view you and does not ruin your relationships.<br /> <br /> :-p","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T06:29:31-07:00","id":558158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=557934#post557934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're confused (or I am):<br /> <br /> The Blessing kicks in when <b>you </b>threaten or use violence on <b>someone else</b>.<br /> <br /> The Curse kicks in when <b>someone else</b> points out <b>you</b> have been hurt.<br /> <br /> So unless the screams literally shatter your ear drum and then someone points that out to you via sign-language you are good to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went back and re-read the text, expecting to be proven wrong, and find myself re-reading and nodding to your interpretation but also finding that it's actually possible to read both from that grammar structure; the mixed usage of he means that it's hard to tell if the person who's suffering over the loss of the parents is the Ogre or his ex.<br /> <br /> I think you're right, but I think the Curse section could use a rewrite for clarity's (ha) sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T07:50:55-07:00","id":558232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=557784#post557784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was not expecting &amp;quot;I'm A Survivor&amp;quot; to start playing in my head after reading the first paragraph.<br /> <br /> Also, what AA said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I started thinking of <a href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=94ETQ5H7h68&amp;autoplay=1\" target=\"_blank\">this.</a><br /> <br /> Anyway, love this! While all the others are nice, I think it's because they feel like, I don't know, rewrites, new concepts that give different meanings to old archetypes. Ogres, on the other hand, are an extrapolation, all that was awesome about the old Seeming crystalized. But hey, I probably don't know what I'm talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:16:54-07:00","id":558280,"title":"","content":"I'm really loving the Ogres! They're short, sweet, and violent. I really love the Blessing and Curse. It makes me smile and laugh at the image of the macho Ogre pretending they're all tough and nothing hurts them, but they're just denying it or pushing it aside, and their weakness is showing actual feelings. <br /> <br /> <br /> My only complaint is that it feels like there's a lot of emphasis on physical violence with the Ogre. I know it said we could be dealing with other forms of violence, but then we're given the impression that we're falling back onto the Ogre's fists in a lot of cases. I'd suggest adding in bits about a social Ogre inflicting emotional abuse, or a witchtooth-style ogre inflicting curses for their violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:47:38-07:00","id":558418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558019#post558019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh sure. I think in these cases, she's flavourfully presenting a &quot;core example&quot; of a character that fits the mold pretty strongly. IE: This is showing you what a character is like, if that character is defined by her Seeming. Not every character is. In these examples, it's a facet of the character that's permeated every bit of her concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nods.<br /> <br /> I thought it would be something like that, which is good because it means our desires are complimentary.<br /> <br /> I mean, I've already said I <i><i>like</i></i> these core examples. I just want them to be clearly labelled as a core example rather than \u201cmost\u201d or \u201cmany\u201d Darklings/Fairest/Ogres.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558280#post558280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only complaint is that it feels like there's a lot of emphasis on physical violence with the Ogre. I know it said we could be dealing with other forms of violence, but then we're given the impression that we're falling back onto the Ogre's fists in a lot of cases. I'd suggest adding in bits about a social Ogre inflicting emotional abuse, or a witchtooth-style ogre inflicting curses for their violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually ok with the physical violence part. The reason being is that to me I read that as a mystical effect of the seeming. With no heart they cannot control their emotions, and default to baser, physical ways of expression themselves.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if they were emotionally abused by their Keeper &quot;spouse&quot; and ripped their heart out to deal with the heartache but never acted violently before or during their Durence; or if they were a gladiator who ripped out their heart to deal with the guilt of killing the other guy, and thus were able to fight without remorse and win their freedom.<br /> <br /> Both cases; they have no heart and thus trouble relating to others in more complex ways than violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-17-2015, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T11:10:00-07:00","id":558469,"title":"","content":"Ok, now I want to write that charachter.<br /> <br /> <b>The Rather Short Durance of Frank Hudson, Ogre Razorhand</b><br /> <br /> I admit, I'm kind of excited this happened. Who hasn't seen moveies about being sucked into another world and being the chosen one. Ok being forced to fight as a Gladiator isn't the same as being the choesne one, but my job is flipping burgers. When else is something interesting going to happen to me? Plus look at these muscles, the trainers here really know their stuff. I was promised that if I win three fights I can go free, I can't wait to show these babies to the girls back home.<br /> <br /> That was much harder than I thought. Not the fight, he didn't even have a chance. At the end the, king I guess, said I had to kill him and. Oh god, I can still see his face every time I close my else. Look, it's just two more fights. I can do this, and then I can get myself a therapist. I can't be the only guy this has happened too, there has to be a doc who'll believe me.<br /> <br /> Just one more fight. Just one more, I can do this. I can't do this. It feels like my heart's broken, literally, all sharp edges that cut me every time I move. When I close my eyes I see them and my heart just breaks even more. I can't escape, I can't fight... I have to do something about my heart. It's the only way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not very close to the central example I admit, but I hope you'll agree that's a good Ogre Durance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T11:21:08-07:00","id":558478,"title":"","content":"Using an Eliot Spencer quote was genius. It immediately put me in the right headspace for Ogres - angry, violent, bruised and broken people, who have very little choice in the matter.<br /> <br /> The only choice Ogres really have is in who they hurt.<br /> <br /> I love it, 100 stars. The Curse wording was a bit tricky but I figured it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T11:54:15-07:00","id":558518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558418#post558418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually ok with the physical violence part. The reason being is that to me I read that as a mystical effect of the seeming. With no heart they cannot control their emotions, and default to baser, physical ways of expression themselves.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if they were emotionally abused by their Keeper &quot;spouse&quot; and ripped their heart out to deal with the heartache but never acted violently before or during their Durence; or if they were a gladiator who ripped out their heart to deal with the guilt of killing the other guy, and thus were able to fight without remorse and win their freedom.<br /> <br /> Both cases; they have no heart and thus trouble relating to others in more complex ways than violence.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh... as it stands, it already includes other expressions than physical. So, I don't think your view fits already. Plus, isn't it always better to include more than just one way of expressing for more variety?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:00:20-07:00","id":558519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558011#post558011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Darkling write up it really felt like Background and Escape were describing one specific person. The Ogre write up's background section describes the <i>situation</i> Ogres were in (bully victim) rather than their charachter traits (The Darkling backgrounds talks about them as loyal people). As a result it doesn't feel so much like a single charachter.<br /> <br /> That's why you have Xenesis and WyrdHampster praising the new format. It's not a new format, but it still feels like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, sorry for mix up with character concepts numbers. But <b>King Raven's</b> autopsy is correct one - Ogres write-up is centered on things the characters <i><b>endured</b></i>, not <i>who</i> they are. It's very important change - Seemings should be about your narrative in Arcadia, not about traits character have. Because I want to be able to make loyal <b>and</b> disloyal Darklings. Or leading <b>and</b> unleading Fairest. Or any other Seeming - Seemings are stories, are choices now.<br /> <br /> But they <b>are not</b> character psychological traits - or we would end with &quot;always loyal Ventrue&quot; or &quot;morbid Moros&quot; splats. Yes, those are part of character concepts pools, but X-Splats are more about transformation and &quot;common themes&quot; - they are more about <b><i>stories </i></b>of character to this day. Especially with Seemings role as <i>&quot;story character choose over one putted by Keeper&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> So I have a request to developers - <i>please</i>, write 2ED Seemings as stories, <b>not</b> psychological traits. Becuase, like with Ogres, the same stimuli can lead to slightly diffrent results - but those results still are all Ogres characters. They still have one Seeming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558011#post558011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly, I love the core concept that an Ogre escapes by tearing out their heart, and with it their compassion.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, wait, now half of all <i><b>Once Upon a Time</b></i> characters are Ogres, not Fairest? Every other character lost it's heart, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:21:18-07:00","id":558534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558519#post558519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, wait, now half of all <i><b>Once Upon a Time</b></i> characters are Ogres, not Fairest? Every other character lost it's heart, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a balance being missed here, but I haven't watched the show long enough to properly comment on it. But, even from what I've seen, I can soundly say no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:34:49-07:00","id":558564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558534#post558534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a balance being missed here, but I haven't watched the show long enough to properly comment on it. But, even from what I've seen, I can soundly say no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Different universe, different rules. (It's not like violence is the logical consiqunce for getting your heart ripped out)<br /> <br /> That said, Regina absolutely was an Ogre Witchtooth who <i>thought</i> she was a Fairest and tried to act like one. Her mother on the other hand actually was a Fairest, a particularly nasty one. Rumplestiltskin a Wizened Hag (see my Wyrd Sorcery)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:47:16-07:00","id":558573,"title":"","content":"I pointed out in RPGnet that Marv from Sin city is a great example of an Ogre, both pushing away and desperately seeking a non-violent connection to humanity<br /> <br /> (Also, that in the same story Goldie could be a Huntsman)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:12:16-07:00","id":558874,"title":"","content":"So, ummm... Do I tell you guys the really goofy way you can map these new Seemings that makes almost perfect sense, that'll only make sense to some of you? Or, do I keep the conversation on track...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:21:07-07:00","id":558878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558874#post558874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, ummm... Do I tell you guys the really goofy way you can map these new Seemings that makes almost perfect sense, that'll only make sense to some of you? Or, do I keep the conversation on track...</div> </div> </div> </div>If I guess right, what do I win? Because I'm already humming the theme song.<br /> <br /> Thief, Grifter, Mastermind, Hitter. Last is Hacker, and the fact that it ends there is why it's almost perfect.<br /> <br /> Let's go steal a tabletop RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:34:22-07:00","id":558885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558874#post558874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, ummm... Do I tell you guys the really goofy way you can map these new Seemings that makes almost perfect sense, that'll only make sense to some of you? Or, do I keep the conversation on track...</div> </div> </div> </div>I can handle the derailment. On the other hand, you can just explain how each Seeming can be represented by Leverage like fetfet suggested. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:35:00-07:00","id":558887,"title":"","content":"The conversation never stays on the rails. Go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:50:52-07:00","id":558896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558885#post558885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can handle the derailment. On the other hand, you can just explain how each Seeming can be represented by Leverage like fetfet suggested. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ha.<br /> <br /> Sophie's the Fairest. Particularly represented in her relationship with the crew when she temporarily quits the team. Hardison's the Wizened. Parker's the Beast. Eliot, obviously, is the Ogre. Tara's the Darkling. Nate's harder to map. He's not quite our Elemental. But there's a pretty clear argument for it. I'll let people mull over that before trying to explain it. It might give some insight. <br /> <br /> So, my derail: Domon Kasshu from Mobile Fighter G Gundam is an Ogre. I'll leave the debate about the rest of the cast to those familiar. (By the rest of the cast, I mean Rain, Allenby, Argo, Sai, George, and Chibodee. One of them represents the seventh Seeming loosely. I could also make an argument for why Rain fits my eighth Seeming, but that's for later.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:02:08-07:00","id":558900,"title":"","content":"You know, I realized that Loyalist could, itself, be a Seeming now. Their &quot;agency&quot;, if you count it, is being Loyal--they leave arcadia on their keeper's watch and control, defining their story whatever way the Keeper says. In some ways its an anti-seeming, but itd be an interesting mechanical place to stick it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:05:33-07:00","id":558901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558900#post558900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I realized that Loyalist could, itself, be a Seeming now. Their &quot;agency&quot;, if you count it, is being Loyal--they leave arcadia on their keeper's watch and control, defining their story whatever way the Keeper says. In some ways its an anti-seeming, but itd be an interesting mechanical place to stick it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a pretty neat idea. Let me see how that feels for the second draft content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:15:28-07:00","id":558913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558900#post558900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I realized that Loyalist could, itself, be a Seeming now. Their &quot;agency&quot;, if you count it, is being Loyal--they leave arcadia on their keeper's watch and control, defining their story whatever way the Keeper says. In some ways its an anti-seeming, but itd be an interesting mechanical place to stick it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, in fact, a really cool and elegant way of handling things - not to mention it gives Loyalists some teeth because they will have access to parts of Contracts unavailable to standard PCs (which neatly represents Gifts of the True Fae)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:40:24-07:00","id":558942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558900#post558900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I realized that Loyalist could, itself, be a Seeming now. Their &quot;agency&quot;, if you count it, is being Loyal--they leave arcadia on their keeper's watch and control, defining their story whatever way the Keeper says. In some ways its an anti-seeming, but itd be an interesting mechanical place to stick it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Cleverest of Things, you just earned your name today.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:45:53-07:00","id":558944,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was going to play the Gundam game, but the thread got back on track first. Oh well, at least it was by a clever idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T19:06:34-07:00","id":558973,"title":"","content":"I like this, but I'm again curious if there are ways to &quot;grow out of&quot; the Curse. I mean, for all of the Seemings (but especially Ogres and Darkings), it feels like there's a nice story to tell about the person who broke but eventually managed to put themselves back together. However, that seems infeasible if trying to do that is going to keep causing you breaking points all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T20:09:45-07:00","id":559008,"title":"","content":"Up to eight now? Was the concept of the seventh released yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T20:22:27-07:00","id":559014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559008#post559008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Up to eight now? Was the concept of the seventh released yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The seventh is in Dark Eras. I'll maybe tease it soon. The eighth is just an idea I have. Something random. Something that I'm not sure will fit into a book. I may write it up as a free thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T20:37:01-07:00","id":559022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559014#post559014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. The seventh is in Dark Eras. I'll maybe tease it soon. The eighth is just an idea I have. Something random. Something that I'm not sure will fit into a book. I may write it up as a free thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm definitely curious to hear more about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T20:58:18-07:00","id":559029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559014#post559014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. The seventh is in Dark Eras. I'll maybe tease it soon. The eighth is just an idea I have. Something random. Something that I'm not sure will fit into a book. I may write it up as a free thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I continue to look forward to learning more of #7 and #8!*<br /> <br /> Hmm, speaking of additional Seemings... Now that it's possible to have Seemings outside the core six from 1e, might the core or (more likely) a supplement give some guidance to those interested in homebrewing a Seeming? I think the support for creating Courts and the short bit on Kith customization have been great, and it would be awesome to go three-for-three with Seemings. Where are your thoughts on it at this time?<br /> <br /> * Not that the interest in #s 5 and 6 is much less; I continue to want to know what tales they tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T21:09:01-07:00","id":559035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558469#post558469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, now I want to write that charachter.<br /> <br /> <b>The Rather Short Durance of Frank Hudson, Ogre Razorhand</b><br /> <br /> I admit, I'm kind of excited this happened. Who hasn't seen moveies about being sucked into another world and being the chosen one. Ok being forced to fight as a Gladiator isn't the same as being the choesne one, but my job is flipping burgers. When else is something interesting going to happen to me? Plus look at these muscles, the trainers here really know their stuff. I was promised that if I win three fights I can go free, I can't wait to show these babies to the girls back home.<br /> <br /> That was much harder than I thought. Not the fight, he didn't even have a chance. At the end the, king I guess, said I had to kill him and. Oh god, I can still see his face every time I close my else. Look, it's just two more fights. I can do this, and then I can get myself a therapist. I can't be the only guy this has happened too, there has to be a doc who'll believe me.<br /> <br /> Just one more fight. Just one more, I can do this. I can't do this. It feels like my heart's broken, literally, all sharp edges that cut me every time I move. When I close my eyes I see them and my heart just breaks even more. I can't escape, I can't fight... I have to do something about my heart. It's the only way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not very close to the central example I admit, but I hope you'll agree that's a good Ogre Durance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang :/. Posts like this one reminds me just how heartbreaking this game can be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T21:10:36-07:00","id":559036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558900#post558900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I realized that Loyalist could, itself, be a Seeming now. Their &quot;agency&quot;, if you count it, is being Loyal--they leave arcadia on their keeper's watch and control, defining their story whatever way the Keeper says. In some ways its an anti-seeming, but itd be an interesting mechanical place to stick it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gain Clarity through completing a task for their Liege. Lose it through disobedience. Access to unique Contract Clauses - I love it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T21:50:09-07:00","id":559048,"title":"","content":"Now that I've had time to digest, this writeup is good. I like it and it does what it needs to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558900#post558900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I realized that Loyalist could, itself, be a Seeming now. Their &quot;agency&quot;, if you count it, is being Loyal--they leave arcadia on their keeper's watch and control, defining their story whatever way the Keeper says. In some ways its an anti-seeming, but itd be an interesting mechanical place to stick it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I was a bit down on the whole Loyalists lacking a seeming thing, but this is so cool I want it to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:53:28-07:00","id":559320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558896#post558896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ha.<br /> <br /> Sophie's the Fairest. Particularly represented in her relationship with the crew when she temporarily quits the team. Hardison's the Wizened. Parker's the Beast. Eliot, obviously, is the Ogre. Tara's the Darkling. Nate's harder to map. He's not quite our Elemental. But there's a pretty clear argument for it. I'll let people mull over that before trying to explain it. It might give some insight.<br /> <br /> So, my derail: Domon Kasshu from Mobile Fighter G Gundam is an Ogre. I'll leave the debate about the rest of the cast to those familiar. (By the rest of the cast, I mean Rain, Allenby, Argo, Sai, George, and Chibodee. One of them represents the seventh Seeming loosely. I could also make an argument for why Rain fits my eighth Seeming, but that's for later.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could argue for Nate being the Darkling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:17:21-07:00","id":559346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559036#post559036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gain Clarity through completing a task for their Liege. Lose it through disobedience. Access to unique Contract Clauses - I love it!</div> </div> </div> </div> The question becomes... can regular Lost purchase the Loyalist Contracts? That would be interesting to ponder. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:24:41-07:00","id":559349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559320#post559320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you could argue for Nate being the Darkling.</div> </div> </div> </div>He'd fit pretty well as a Darkling. Particularly in his dealings with Hardison, and all those interesting trust/betrayal dynamics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T08:27:52-07:00","id":559396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559346#post559346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The question becomes... can regular Lost purchase the Loyalist Contracts? That would be interesting to ponder.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what Dave's said about Seeming clauses,* anyone can learn them if they're either a member of that Seeming or get a member of that Seeming to teach them how to use it. I think it would be best to keep the Loyalist Seeming playing by the same rules. There's just a really interesting context around non-Loyalists have learned to use them. It could indicate Loyalist sympathies or a sign that one gave into temptation to a Loyalist's bargaining chip, for instance. Or, if it's possible for one to gain or change a Seeming under particular or unusual circumstances,** it could be an ex-Loyalist one's looking at, there.<br /> <br /> * No formal name's materialized for the Seeming-specific Contract bonuses, so I'm just going to keep calling them this until one does. Or it becomes clear that &quot;clause&quot; is reserved for something else.<br /> <br /> ** Seemingless Changelings having some means of acquiring a Seeming is a thought I had some time ago. It may or may not fit for members of the original six Seemings to change into one other, but someone going from one of those six to Loyalist and vice-versa potentially feels right to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:16:31-07:00","id":559507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558900#post558900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I realized that Loyalist could, itself, be a Seeming now. Their &quot;agency&quot;, if you count it, is being Loyal--they leave arcadia on their keeper's watch and control, defining their story whatever way the Keeper says. In some ways its an anti-seeming, but itd be an interesting mechanical place to stick it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have other question with this idea - if Seemings change your Mien enough to make recognizable marks on it ( i.e. Darkling Mien become scary and dark, Fairest are, literally, bright and shinny ) would not Loyalist Seeming mark you obviously as the Gentry agent? How could Loyalist then inflirtrate Chageling's Freeholds and be &quot;secret threat&quot;? And what kind of Loyalist Seeming would their Mien got then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-18-2015, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:22:44-07:00","id":559523,"title":"","content":"<i>Unless</i> the marks a Loyalist seeming leaves on you look like another seeming.<br /> <br /> Stealth mode Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:33:23-07:00","id":559532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=558973#post558973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this, but I'm again curious if there are ways to &quot;grow out of&quot; the Curse. I mean, for all of the Seemings (but especially Ogres and Darkings), it feels like there's a nice story to tell about the person who broke but eventually managed to put themselves back together. However, that seems infeasible if trying to do that is going to keep causing you breaking points all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the Ogre has an out; if he realizes he's hurting <i>on his own terms, </i>it's a wound that can't be reopened.<br /> <br /> Can we make that obvious?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T11:05:15-07:00","id":559570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559532#post559532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the Ogre has an out; if he realizes he's hurting <i>on his own terms, </i>it's a wound that can't be reopened.<br /> <br /> Can we make that obvious?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunh. I actually kinda feel like it might make sense to make explicit that an Ogre <i>can't</i> just do that to avoid the Curse. Otherwise Ogres are encouraged to be really open about how they're hurting. I mean, when the start of the sentence is, &quot;Despite their outward appearance and [insistence]* otherwise, Ogres do feel pain just like anyone else,&quot; it feels really at odds that the best means of avoiding the Curse would be opening up to anyone and everyone instead of trying to hide or deny it. That doesn't feel like the kind of behavior this archetype is meant to incentivize.<br /> <br /> * This was &quot;instance,&quot; but &quot;insistence&quot; is the only word I can think of that feels like a natural fit here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T11:17:30-07:00","id":559577,"title":"","content":"I mean, that approach requires an awful lot of self awareness. I'm ok with that being a way to deal with the Curse that plays against type. It would be an interesting roleplaying challenge to portray an Ogre who bears the shattered fragments of his heart on his sleeve and still comes across as Ogre-like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T12:11:49-07:00","id":559658,"title":"","content":"So in regards to this Loyalist Seeming. I'm not sold on it thematically; Seeming is how you took control of the story and Loyalists typically did not. Now if you drew a distinction between someone abducted specifically for a job on Earth and still follows their role and someone who was supposed to be a slave but talked their way up into being an agent; that would be different.<br /> <br /> Is there going to be some sort of way to transend your seeming? A loyalist seeming just screams out for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559577#post559577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, that approach requires an awful lot of self awareness. I'm ok with that being a way to deal with the Curse that plays against type. It would be an interesting roleplaying challenge to portray an Ogre who bears the shattered fragments of his heart on his sleeve and still comes across as Ogre-like.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO that's true of the entire Seeming. Fairest for example loose Clairty for something that happens. Bob got hurt, that's an easy thing to understand. Ogres loose Clarity for something they feel; that's much harder to call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-18-2015, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T13:47:38-07:00","id":559754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559346#post559346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The question becomes... can regular Lost purchase the Loyalist Contracts? That would be interesting to ponder.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd suggest &quot;Yes, but they sacrifice Clarity every time they use them&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:50:26-07:00","id":559814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559658#post559658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO that's true of the entire Seeming. Fairest for example loose Clairty for something that happens. Bob got hurt, that's an easy thing to understand. Ogres loose Clarity for something they feel; that's much harder to call.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant self-awareness on the character's part. The character doesn't need to be aware of his own vulnerabilities for the player to be aware of them. It will certainly require the player to be roleplaying in good faith either way. But for the character to confront their vulnerabilities on their own (so as to avoid the Breaking Point when someone else makes them realize they are in pain) necessitates the character being self-aware enough to know what his own triggers are. Definitely a challenging character to play either way, but because of that I'm personally not bothered that the latter approach can be used to effectively avoid the Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:08:36-07:00","id":559987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559349#post559349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He'd fit pretty well as a Darkling. Particularly in his dealings with Hardison, and all those interesting trust/betrayal dynamics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still trying to figure out what the Elemental argument is. I need to rewatch Leverage. I hope you're happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:25:06-07:00","id":560018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fetfet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559987#post559987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still trying to figure out what the Elemental argument is. I need to rewatch Leverage. I hope you're happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rewatching Leverage is always the right choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:21:56-07:00","id":560273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=560018#post560018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rewatching Leverage is always the right choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>So when are we going to get an announcement of: &quot;Let's go steal an Onyx Path RPG&quot;? :P (Yes, I'm aware of the other one my MWP)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=559658#post559658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in regards to this Loyalist Seeming. I'm not sold on it thematically; Seeming is how you took control of the story and Loyalists typically did not. Now if you drew a distinction between someone abducted specifically for a job on Earth and still follows their role and someone who was supposed to be a slave but talked their way up into being an agent; that would be different.<br /> <br /> Is there going to be some sort of way to transend your seeming? A loyalist seeming just screams out for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit, when put in that sort of viewpoint there's no strong argument against being able to change seemings - A seeming fits a type of agency much more tightly this go around and a person's type of agency can change as they age, mature and gain life experiences. Realistically, Loyalists *do* have agency, just not in the same way as your PCs do - at their core they're people have accepted their fate and that's their agency. The old idiom of &quot;Power to change what I can, accept what I can't change and wisdom to know the difference&quot; pretty much feels like the 'core' of the Loyalist mould.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:30:37-07:00","id":560281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=560273#post560273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So when are we going to get an announcement of: &quot;Let's go steal an Onyx Path RPG&quot;? :P (Yes, I'm aware of the other one my MWP)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm biased. I did a ton of work on that game. The Hitter chapter in the Player's Guide is some of my all-time favorite work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:37:27-07:00","id":560286,"title":"","content":"Oh!<br /> <br /> Well, that definitely explains a lot. I love the show and own the book, but I still haven't had a chance to actually play a game of it yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T16:36:58-07:00","id":561326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=560018#post560018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rewatching Leverage is always the right choice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right up until you get to the end, then it's very sad that its over... again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T22:04:55-07:00","id":561561,"title":"","content":"Damn, I just got the best idea for Loyalist only Contracts (others can learn them with a Loyalist or Gentry teacher, but unlike Loyalists they hemorrhage Clarity by using them)... but I actually want to submit them as an application... except I don't know how Second Edition Contract mechanics work so I can't!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T00:50:16-07:00","id":563797,"title":"","content":"Okay, awesome seeming, as it expands on the concept from the original in a really elegant way. <br /> <br /> Also? For an example of a non-physical Ogre, I'd actually say the teacher from Whiplash(at least what I've seen of him in clips from the movie.) Because... well, someone that verbally abusive fits the Ogre as presented(may be missing aspects of his character that go against this however.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T04:32:41-07:00","id":563966,"title":"","content":"After playing through the latest episode of Game of Thrones The Telltale game it struck me that one of their characters fits the ogre seeming very much.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/MUNvjqMQRJ4?t=43m23s\" target=\"_blank\">Minor spoiler, don't clickety if you don't want to see!</a><br /> Shortly put, it's one of the characters getting pissed because they want to go where the main character is going. They get drunk and try and beat you up. When they finally recover they tell you why they aren't all too hyped to enter the city. Their background and their way of dealing with it struck me as particularily ogre-ish. If you don't intend to play the game or if you don't mind a minor spoiler, then I'd suggest taking a peek at the scene. It's very nicely done and hits hard to home because the narrative has made you like this character quite a bit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T16:53:21-07:00","id":564748,"title":"","content":"Oddly, loyalists could even have Courts. I mean, with the new make-your-own Court rules, not only can Loyalist itself be a seeming, but each gentry can have a Court to represent the changelings under its keeping. some things like Approaches wouldnt work, but Mantles and Contracts tailored to your keeper's changeling slaves, above and beyond kith and seeming benefits, really does give Loyalists a very disturbingly alien, yet scarily recognizable, structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T17:30:53-07:00","id":564775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=564748#post564748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some things like Approaches wouldnt work</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I can see how they might. Loyalists are in league with the Strangers, but that's not really accurate: a <i>particular </i>Loyalist is in league with a <i>particular </i>Stranger. The Gentry aren't all one big happy family, after all. A rival True Fae could well see the Loyalist servants of another as impressive prizes and sources of leverage. I doubt the Huntsmen discriminate between an old master and a prospective one, if the latter can make it worth their while. Given the Strangers' generous definition of sanity, I could even see the Loyalist's own Keeper dispatching a Huntsman, whether as a test to &quot;cull the unworthy,&quot; a punishment for some (quasi-)imagined offense or other anticipated action, or even just a rescinding of the previous distant arrangement and a decision to bring the Loyalist &quot;home.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:34:59-07:00","id":564929,"title":"","content":"As a dark irony, a particularly well ranked Loyalist in a mad arcadian court might be able to inflict their personal approaches onto a Changeling, a dark mirror of their own faults and abuse being perpetrated on those with the gaul to go free. Thus, most changelings fear their own approaches, and those of their Court, blissfully unaware that their own loyal kin have a way of contuining arcadia's mythcycle and trickery without their permission simply by the fact that they, too, were once human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:51:54-07:00","id":564949,"title":"","content":"Sorry to double post (and due to derailment, it may be best to make a Loyalist as Seeming/Courts thread), but I was pondering the whole.. Seeming affects appearance thing. I think it should definitely not be a distinctive look, but rather the mutability of Arcadia shines through in their mein. While Loyalists might have the striking Arcadian mesh and chaos of features of undefined symbolism, its not unusual for non-loyalist changelings to look seeming-ambiguous or at least the seeming equivalent of androgyny (&quot;youre a beast? Wow, im sorry, ive thought you were an ogre for months&quot;, or &quot;I hate to be rude.. youre beautiful, but may I ask.. are you Fairest or Elemental?&quot;. ) . Itd look and seem flexible enough most Loyalists could pass themselves off as whatever Seeming suits their task at hand. Since seeming is more about psychology and contract tweaks rather than built in obvious blessings, i assume that also means even morseo in 2e that seeming confusion will be a thing--loyalists, like the Deceived of mummy, capitalize on that. It may require a full on Pledge to out a Loyalist, and you can be sure their masters taught them how to make pledges that cover their butts and can turn against the Freehold if the loyalist is discovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T20:48:36-07:00","id":566016,"title":"","content":"Sweet sugar cakes, it's finally out and I almost missed it!<br /> <br /> I was a bit curious what it meant saying Ogres were about consumption and the current write up didn't really explain what that meant. I love the Ogre concept that they took too much abuse and finally just lashed out at people, and the whole ripping out their heart thing is amazing. Not only is it symbolic, but it shows the Ogre sinking to the depths of insanity where they rip themselves apart just for some measure of relief.<br /> <br /> As for those who are confused about Ogres having poor social skills, I interpret it to be that Ogres are the Changelings who lack a profanity filter on what they say and do. They speak what's on their mind, always, and if you have a problem with it, feel free to tell them so... to their face.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also love how Ogres don't need to be hulking brutes and yet can still focus on brute force over finesse. Ogres who don't like getting their hands dirty can make for some very controversial allies, especially when they have the enemy caught in a moment of weakness and decide to blow up the area <b>with their motley still inside</b> because they don't want to risk the target escaping.<br /> <br /> Of course the sacrifices likely aren't aware of this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}